\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 **Cosmic Compendium Entry: Travel through The Convergence**\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 In The Convergence, there are two primary methods of travel: conventional and arcane\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Conventional travel involves moving along the 'surface' of the donut, from one point to another. This can take a considerable amount of time, even with advanced faster-than-light technologies, due to the immense distances involved.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Arcane travel, on the other hand, involves 'cutting' through the donut. It is achieved by using ancient artifacts known as Portal Keys, which can open gateways in the fabric of space-time, allowing for near-instantaneous travel between two points. These artifacts are rare and highly sought after, as they provide a strategic advantage for exploration, trade, and warfare.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Bifrost which has been in use throughout The Convergence for some time now is a form of "Arcane Travel".\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 However, arcane travel isn't without risks. Misuse of a Portal Key can lead to disastrous consequences, including being lost in the interstitial space between realities, or worse, attracting the attention of the enigmatic beings that dwell in those liminal spaces.}